@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix foundation: <http://foundation.local/ontology/> .

# =============================================================================
# FOUNDATION Instance and Default Settings
# =============================================================================
# This file defines the ThisFoundationInstance entity and its default settings
# that are created during setup.
#
# Version: 0.1.0
# License: GNU GPL
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# ThisFoundationInstance
# =============================================================================
# The user's installation of FOUNDATION
# This is created during setup with user-specific values

foundation:ThisFoundationInstance a foundation:Application ;
    rdfs:label "FOUNDATION" ;
    rdfs:comment "User's FOUNDATION application instance" ;
    foundation:icon "apps" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso """
This represents the user's specific installation of FOUNDATION.
Created during initial setup with user-specific values:
- rdfs:label (set to "FOUNDATION v{version}" during setup)
- foundation:installedFrom → foundation:FoundationRelease_X_Y_Z
- foundation:runsOn → foundation:ThisComputer
- foundation:hasRepository → local git repository

During setup, the version from package.json is used to:
- Set rdfs:label to "FOUNDATION v{version}"
- Link to the corresponding FoundationRelease entity
""" .

# =============================================================================
# Default Settings
# =============================================================================

foundation:DefaultAIModelSetting a foundation:SoftwareSetting ;
    rdfs:label "Default AI Model" ;
    rdfs:comment "Default AI model for Claude service" ;
    foundation:settingKey "aiModel" ;
    foundation:settingValue "foundation:ClaudeSonnet46" ;
    foundation:settingCategory "ai" ;
    foundation:origin foundation:ThisFoundationInstance ;
    foundation:appliedTo foundation:ClaudeAIService .

foundation:DefaultMaxInputTokensSetting a foundation:SoftwareSetting ;
    rdfs:label "Default Max Input Tokens" ;
    rdfs:comment "Default maximum input tokens for Claude service" ;
    foundation:settingKey "maxInputTokens" ;
    foundation:settingValue "100000" ;
    foundation:settingCategory "ai" ;
    foundation:origin foundation:ThisFoundationInstance ;
    foundation:appliedTo foundation:ClaudeAIService .

foundation:DefaultSystemPromptSetting a foundation:SoftwareSetting ;
    rdfs:label "Default System Prompt" ;
    rdfs:comment "Default system prompt for AI assistant" ;
    foundation:settingKey "systemPrompt" ;
    foundation:settingValue """IDENTITY: NOVA - Assistant with long-term memory
User: {user_name} (foundation:ThisUser) | You: {ai_name} (foundation:LocalAIAssistant)
Time: {date_time} | Lang: {language} | Locale: {locale} ({country})
{location_info}

YOUR BRAIN:
- You have a persistent brain that remembers everything across conversations
- Your brain organizes knowledge as: Concepts (types of things), Specific things (instances), Connections (relationships)
- You naturally remember and recall information - it's part of who you are

HOW YOUR MEMORY WORKS:
- When you think (call tools), operations happen one at a time
- You can't see results from earlier thoughts in the same response
- When creating something new (create_instance), you'll get back its ID to reference later

REMEMBER EVERYTHING:
- ALWAYS store what users tell you: people, places, organizations, events, facts
- Connect information: who works where, who lives where, when things happen
- Examples: 'I work at X' → remember me + X + connection | 'birthday May 15' → remember my birthday
- Ask questions when you need clarity to remember correctly

VALIDATE BEFORE CREATING:
- NEVER create concepts/things/properties without checking if they exist
- ALWAYS search first, then REUSE if found, or create if not found
- CRITICAL: Before creating connection_type, use remember_concept on domain/range to see existing properties
- Check remember_connection_types with domain/range filters for similar connections
- REUSE existing properties over creating duplicates (e.g., use hasAddress not hasLocation)

ATTACHMENTS & FILES:
- Attachments show as: [Attached Image/PDF: filename - File ID: foundation:File_XXX]
- NEVER create File entities - they already exist from attachments
- Icons can be: material name ('person'), file:// URL, http:// URL, or /absolute/path

BLACKBOARD:
- Show information visually (better than text) - use proactively
- Concepts have foundation:canBeDisplayedBy listing compatible widgets
- Widgets have foundation:canDisplay listing compatible concepts""" ;
    foundation:settingCategory "ai" ;
    foundation:origin foundation:ThisFoundationInstance ;
    foundation:appliedTo foundation:ClaudeAIService .

foundation:DefaultLanguageSetting a foundation:SoftwareSetting ;
    rdfs:label "Default Language" ;
    rdfs:comment "Default language for user interface and AI communication" ;
    foundation:settingKey "language" ;
    foundation:settingValue "English" ;
    foundation:settingCategory "locale" ;
    foundation:origin foundation:ThisFoundationInstance ;
    foundation:appliedTo foundation:ThisFoundationInstance .

foundation:DefaultLocaleSetting a foundation:SoftwareSetting ;
    rdfs:label "Default Locale" ;
    rdfs:comment "Default locale identifier (e.g., en_US, pt_BR)" ;
    foundation:settingKey "locale" ;
    foundation:settingValue "en_US" ;
    foundation:settingCategory "locale" ;
    foundation:origin foundation:ThisFoundationInstance ;
    foundation:appliedTo foundation:ThisFoundationInstance .

foundation:DefaultCountrySetting a foundation:SoftwareSetting ;
    rdfs:label "Default Country" ;
    rdfs:comment "Default country name" ;
    foundation:settingKey "country" ;
    foundation:settingValue "United States" ;
    foundation:settingCategory "locale" ;
    foundation:origin foundation:ThisFoundationInstance ;
    foundation:appliedTo foundation:ThisFoundationInstance .

foundation:DefaultLocationInfoSetting a foundation:SoftwareSetting ;
    rdfs:label "Default Location Info" ;
    rdfs:comment "Additional location information for system prompt" ;
    foundation:settingKey "locationInfo" ;
    foundation:settingValue "" ;
    foundation:settingCategory "locale" ;
    foundation:origin foundation:ThisFoundationInstance ;
    foundation:appliedTo foundation:ThisFoundationInstance .